Sentence 1: Varaždin Generalate The Varaždin Generalate (, ), also known as the "Windische Grenze" ("Wendian/Wendish [Slavic] Border") in German, was a Habsburg Monarchy Military Frontier province centred in Warasdin (Varaždin), Kingdom of Croatia within Habsburg Monarchy, that existed between 1531 and the 18th century.
