Sentence 1: By the 1560s the Habsburgs established a frontier defense system, made up of six main "Grenzgeneralat" (captain-generalcies) in the Military Frontier in Hungary and Croatia, each commanded by captain generals; the one centred in Varaždin was after 1578 known as the Wendish-Bajcsavár captain-generalcy.
